CORE
deep-operand-chain.smt2

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^sat$
--
^\(error
--
Regression test for handling deeply nested input without unbounded recursion
anywhere in the pipeline. A deeply right-associated operand chain
`(bvand x (bvand x (bvand x ... x)))` of depth 3500 is parsed and solved (sat)
without overflowing the call stack: the SMT2 expression parser, the boolbvt
bit-vector conversion and irept destruction all avoid per-level recursion. A
recursive implementation segfaults on this input, including on the small
(~1 MiB) default stack used on some platforms (e.g. Visual Studio); the test is
run as CORE so those small-stack configurations are exercised.
